Version: 1.1
desc: Peak Performance Clipper (PeakEater port) by chmaha
tags: processing clipper waveshaper saturation limiter peak oversampling
author: chmaha
changelog:
  Add full copyright and licence header (upstream authors' notices).
about:
  A wave-shaping peak clipper. The input is boosted by the ceiling amount, shaped by one of eight curves (Hard,
  Quintic, Cubic, Tangent, Algebraic, Arctangent, Sine, or Custom with an adjustable knee) and brought back down,
  optionally at up to 32x oversampling with linear-phase half-band filters. A scrolling peak analyser shows what
  goes in and what is eaten. Beyond the original: a ceiling guard that stops oversampling overshoot, a delta
  switch to hear only what is removed, emphasis/de-emphasis tilt around a pivot frequency, a ceiling/output link,
  a display range above 0 dB and a time zoom, and fixes for the start-up fade-in, the high-frequency phase shift
  of the oversampler, the dry/wet alignment, the oversampling switch click, the sine curve and the Eaten reading.
  Ported from PeakEater by Vladyslav Voinov
  https://github.com/vvvar/PeakEater (GPL-3.0)
  JSFX version released under GPL-3.0 license
  Claude generated some of this code
